##
  Description: Classifies the process-owned inverse ledger named by a recovery token.
  Evolution: Closed; recovery authority kind changes require an ABI-major release.
  Invariant: OpenRollback is valid only for failed-open rollback and CloseRestore only for failed-cleanup restoration.
##
@abi_type_id(0x540000000000002d)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public type TerminalRecoveryLedgerKind:
    OpenRollback = 1
    CloseRestore = 2

##
  Description: Owns the process terminal pair, restoration ledger, and one unissued process-recovery generation reservation with compiler-enforced affine ownership and a runtime-validated state machine.
  Invariant: using owns the binding; ordinary calls borrow it; direct close mutates it to Closed only on success. A successful open moves one exclusive unissued recovery-generation reservation into the binding; it remains attached through Active, Paused, and RestorePending until clean close releases it or failed lexical cleanup consumes it to issue CloseRestore authority. Observable binding states are Active, Paused, RestorePending, and Closed; Opening and failed recovery are coordinator-only.
##
@abi_type_id(0x540000000000002e)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public compiler_registered affine resource type TerminalSession

##
  Description: Is a sealed opaque immutable alias to one process-owned recovery capability cell after an ownership epoch consumes its reserved generation capacity.
  Invariant: Construction is runtime-only and occurs only when failed-open rollback or failed lexical cleanup consumes that epoch's exclusive reservation. Aliases share one authenticated coordinator, ledger identity, kind, issued generation, claim, and consumed state. It exposes no host handle, session identity, reservation, or ledger contents.
  Evolution: Closed; authority semantics and representation change only in an ABI-major release.
##
@abi_type_id(0x540000000000002f)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public opaque immutable type TerminalRecoveryToken

##
  Description: Names the process coordinator ownership and recovery state for the standard terminal pair.
  Invariant: Free-to-Opening preflights and exclusively installs one unissued process-recovery generation reservation before Opening publication, lease-epoch replacement, inspection, mutation, ledger insertion, or ownership exposure. Opening and failed recovery states never expose a TerminalSession binding; Free means no process-owned terminal ledger or live reservation, and Active, Paused, or RestorePending have exactly one live binding carrying the reservation. Successful close releases an unused reservation; successful recovery leaves its issued generation permanently spent and returns the coordinator to Free. A directly closed binding may remain inspectable as TerminalSessionState.Closed without coordinator ownership.
  Evolution: Closed; additions require an ABI-major release.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000030)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public type TerminalCoordinatorState:
    Free = 1
    Opening = 2
    Active = 3
    Paused = 4
    RestorePending = 5
    FailedOpenRecovery = 6
    FailedCloseRecovery = 7

##
  Description: Represents whether a structured diagnostic observed no binding state or one observable TerminalSession state.
  Invariant: Unavailable records the absence of a session binding; all other variants correspond exactly to public binding states.
  Evolution: Closed; additions require an ABI-major release.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000031)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public type TerminalDiagnosticSessionState:
    Unavailable = 1
    Active = 2
    Paused = 3
    RestorePending = 4
    Closed = 5

##
  Description: Is nominal application-reviewed terminal output; construction is the explicit trust boundary.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000032)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(standard_library)
public opaque immutable type TrustedTerminalOutput

##
  Description: Is escaped bounded diagnostic output safe for terminal display and never contains active control sequences.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000033)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(standard_library)
public opaque immutable type SafeTerminalDiagnosticOutput

##
  Description: Is an immutable runtime-origin sequence of pause-delivered events.
  Invariant: Every successful Active-to-Paused transition ends in exactly one PauseBoundary reset.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000034)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public opaque immutable type TerminalPauseEvents

##
  Description: Is an immutable runtime-origin bounded diagnostic collection with deterministic order and truncation metadata.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000035)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
@constructor_visibility(runtime)
public opaque immutable type TerminalDiagnosticCollection

##
  Description: Is an immutable opaque options snapshot built from stable ABI-major defaults and functional with_* calls.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000036)
@abi_evolution(additive_opaque)
@constructor_visibility(standard_library)
public opaque immutable type TerminalSessionOptions

##
  Description: Configures v1 terminal feature requests as one application-constructible policy snapshot.
  Invariant: Trusted-paste policy is backend-independent and does not require bracketed-paste transport.
  Evolution: Closed; new feature categories use new additive option APIs rather than changing this record.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000037)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
public type TerminalSessionFeaturePolicy:
    use_alternate_screen: boolean
    hide_cursor: boolean
    enable_bracketed_paste: boolean
    require_trusted_paste_framing: boolean
    enable_enhanced_key_identity: boolean
    enable_focus_events: boolean
    mouse_tracking: TerminalMouseTracking
    capture_control_keys: boolean
    require_requested_features: boolean

##
  Description: Configures all v1 parser, payload, correlation, diagnostic, and retention limits.
  Evolution: Closed; new resource categories use new additive option APIs rather than changing this record.
##
@abi_type_id(0x5400000000000038)
@abi_evolution(closed_major_only)
public type TerminalSessionResourceLimits:
    input_sequence_timeout: TerminalInputSequenceTimeoutMilliseconds
    maximum_committed_text_bytes: TerminalCommittedTextByteLimit
    maximum_composition_preedit_bytes: TerminalCompositionPreeditByteLimit
    maximum_paste_chunk_bytes: TerminalPasteChunkByteLimit
    maximum_unknown_chunk_bytes: TerminalUnknownByteChunkLimit
    maximum_pending_sequence_bytes: TerminalPendingSequenceByteLimit
    maximum_retained_events: TerminalRetainedEventLimit
    maximum_retained_bytes: TerminalRetainedByteLimit
    maximum_correlated_events: TerminalCorrelatedEventLimit
    maximum_correlated_bytes: TerminalCorrelatedByteLimit
    maximum_diagnostics: TerminalDiagnosticCountLimit
    maximum_diagnostic_bytes: TerminalDiagnosticCollectionByteLimit

