##
  Description: Reports terminal-session open failures and resume failures that occur before mutation or after complete live-binding compensation.
  Invariant: GenerationExhausted is emitted only by initial Free acquisition when capacity for one future process-recovery generation cannot be reserved; it occurs before Opening publication, lease-epoch replacement, terminal inspection/mutation, ledger insertion, or ownership exposure. RollbackFailed is open-only and, with RecoveryPending, carries a sealed alias to process-owned recovery authority. ResumeFailed carries no token and leaves the live binding Paused because resume made no mutation or completely rolled back every mutation.
  Evolution: Additive error family; unknown variants propagate by stable family and variant identity.
##
