##
  Description: Reports live-binding restoration/compensation failure and authenticated process-owned recovery rejection; successful close notices are not errors.
  Invariant: ResumeRestorePending carries ordered diagnostics but no recovery token because the live binding retains its shortened inverse ledger, unissued reservation, and retry authority in RestorePending. Failed-open and failed-cleanup transfer consume the ownership epoch's pre-reserved capacity, so this family has no generation-exhaustion emission. Process-owned retryable pending failures return an alias to the same issued-generation sealed recovery token. WrongSession, WrongKind, Stale, Consumed, and RecoveryInProgress reject before terminal mutation or authority consumption.
